  "text_blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "snippet": "Common and active scams reported across Central Illinois include:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "snippet": "Top Active Scams in Central Illinois"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "list": [
        {
          "snippet": "AI Voice & Imposter Scams: Scammers use artificial intelligence voice cloning to impersonate family members in distress or pose as government officials, law enforcement (such as the FBI or U.S. Attorneys), and the IRS.",
          "reference_indexes": [
            0,
            1,
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "snippet": "Phishing & Text Smishing: Fake text messages impersonating the Illinois Secretary of State, traffic/toll courts, or the Central Violations Bureau threaten license suspensions or fines and use QR links to steal data.",
          "reference_indexes": [
            3,
            4,
            5
          ]
        },
        {
          "snippet": "Home Repair & Storm Chasers: Door-to-door contractors offer quick roof repairs, driveway sealing, or free storm damage inspections after severe weather, demanding large cash advances or full upfront payment before disappearing.",
          "reference_indexes": [
            6,
            7
          ]
        },
        {
          "snippet": "Romance & Social Media Shopping Scams: Fraudsters build fake online relationships to steal money or create social media accounts with heavily discounted fake offers for trending products."
        },
        {
          "snippet": "Traditional Cons: Prize offers, fake travel packages, bogus health/vitamin products, recovery scams, and charity solicitations.",
          "reference_indexes": [
            8
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "snippet": "How to Protect Yourself"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "list": [
        {
          "snippet": "Establish a family safe word: Agree on a secret code word with family members to verify identities during unexpected or urgent phone calls.",
          "reference_indexes": [
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "snippet": "Practice the pause: If a caller pressures you to act immediately, hang up and verify the claim through an official, independently looked-up phone number.",
          "reference_indexes": [
            10
          ]
        },
        {
          "snippet": "Never pay via untraceable methods: Be suspicious of anyone demanding payment via gift cards, wire transfers, cryptocurrency, peer-to-peer apps, or cash/gold couriers.",
          "reference_indexes": [
            11
          ]
        },
        {
          "snippet": "Verify official websites: Double-check URLs (such as official court or government portals) before entering sensitive financial information."
        }
      ]
    },
